<speak>It is easier to see that habit in someone else than in ourselves, isn't it? Having a few clear boundaries may make the handover feel less like you are abandoning oversight and more like you are giving people room to work. For your personal banking administration, the boundary can remain straightforward: we contact you directly, and routine logistical help from family does not need to become involvement in the substantive conversation. That should leave your nephew free to focus on his own responsibilities. How are you finding the balance between time in the office and time away from it at the moment?</speak>